{
  "title": "Tibial Stress Syndrome (Shin Splints)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3108/tibial-stress-syndrome-shin-splints",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 1 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Tibial stress syndrome (also known as shin splints) is an overuse injury or repetitive-load injury of the shin area that leads to persistent dull anterior leg pain.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with tenderness along the posteromedial distal tibia made worse with plantarflexion. Radiographs or bone scans may be obtained to rule out stress fractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally nonoperative with NSAIDs, rest and activity modifications.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "10-15% of running injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "60% of leg pain syndromes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "medial (posteromedial) tibial stress syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most common",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "anterior (anterolateral) tibial stress syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "distal and posteromedial tibia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "runners without enough **shock absorption** (running on cement or uneven surfaces, improper running shoes)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "training errors (sudden increase in training intensity and duration)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "running >20 miles/week",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hill training early in the season",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "history of previous lower extremity injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**over-pronation or increase internal tibial rotation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**caused by a traction periostitis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "anterolateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "traction periostitis of tibialis anterior on tibia and interosseous membrane",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "posteromedial",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "traction periostitis of tibialis posterior and soleus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**female athlete triad**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**critical to diagnose and treat**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**tibial stress fractures**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "females have 1.5-3.5 increased risk of progression to stress fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "vague, diffuse pain along middle-distal tibia that **decreases** with running (early stage)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "differentiate from exertional compartment syndrome, for which pain increases with running",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "earlier onset of pain with more frequent training (later stages)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "tenderness along posteromedial border of tibia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "4cm proximal to medial malleolus, extending proximally up to 12cm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**pes planus**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**tight Achilles tendon**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**weak core muscles**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative test",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pain on resisted plantar flexion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "exclude stress fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "conventional radiographs are normal in first 2-3weeks",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "long-term changes include **periosteal exostoses**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "differentiate from stress fracture, which shows \"dreaded black line\"",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3108/images/dreaded%20black%20line.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "3-phase bone scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "exclude stress fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**diffuse, longitudinal** increased uptake along posteromedial border of tibia in **delayed phase (Phase 3)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3108/images/bone%20scan%20shin%20splints.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "normal findings on Phase 1 (flow phase) and **blood pool phase (Phase 2)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "differentiate from stress fracture, which has **focal, intense** hyperperfusion and hyperemia in Phase 1 and 2, and focal, fusiform uptake in Phase 3",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3108/images/stress%20fracture%20bone%20scan.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "identify other soft tissue injuries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3108/images/mri%20shin%20splints.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "periosteal edema",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "progressive marrow involvment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 3,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Differential Diagnosis for Exertional Leg Pain**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "*Condition*",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "*Characteristics*",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Tissue origin",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Anterior tibial stress syndrome",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Vague, diffuse pain along anterolateral tibia, worse at beginning of exercise that **decreases during training**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Periosteum",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Medial tibial stress syndrome",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Vague, diffuse pain along middle-distal tibia, worse at beginning of exercise, that **decreases during training**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Periosteum",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Tibial/fibular stress fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Pain with running, **point tenderness** over fracture site, \"dreaded black line\" on lateral x-ray",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Bone",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Exertional compartment syndrome",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Symptoms begin 10min into exercise and**resolve 30min after exercise**, sensory or motor loss, elevated anterior compartment pressures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Muscle and fascia",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Leg Tendinopathy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "May be Achilles tendon, peroneal tendon, or tibialis posterior",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Tendon",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Sural or SPN entrapment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Dermatomal distribution of symptoms",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Nerve",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Lumbar radiculopathy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Worse with lumbar tension position (sitting)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Nerve",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Popliteal artery entrapment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Diagnosed with vascular studies",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Blood vessel",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**activity modification with nonoperative modalities**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment and successful in vast majority",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "techniques",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "activity modification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "decreasing running distance, frequency and intensity by 50%",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "use low-impact and cross-training exercises during rehab period",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "regular stretching and strengthening",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "run on synthetic track",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "avoid running on hills, uneven or hard surfaces",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "shoe modifications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "change running shoes every 250-500miles as shoes lose shock absorbing capacity at this distance",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "orthotics may be helpful in patients with pes planus",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "therapy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "focus on **strengthening of invertors and evertors of the calf**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "other",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**local phonophoresis with corticosteroids may be effective**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "deep posterior compartment fasciotomy + release of painful portion of periosteum",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
